(Nimbus Technologies is a software company headquartered in Pune, India, with offices in) '
(Bengaluru and Hyderabad. This handbook applies to all full-time employees. Part-time employees) '
(and interns follow a separate policy document issued by the HR team.) '
() '
(Standard working hours are 9:30 am to 6:30 pm, Monday to Friday, including a one-hour lunch) '
(break. Employees may choose flexible hours, starting any time between 8:00 am and 11:00 am, as) '
(long as they complete 8 working hours each day. Core hours, when every employee must be) '
(available for meetings, are 11:00 am to 4:00 pm.) '
() '
(Employees may work from home up to 2 days per week. Working from home on more than 2 days in a) '
(week requires written approval from the reporting manager. During the first 3 months of) '
(employment, work from home is limited to 1 day per week.) '
() '
(Attendance is recorded through the Nimbus HR portal. Employees must mark attendance before) '
(11:30 am. Three late attendance marks in a single month will be counted as half a day of leave.) '
(Employees who are unable to come to work must inform their manager by email or chat before) '
(10:00 am.) '
() '
(Overtime is not paid for employees at grade L4 and above. Employees at grades L1 to L3 who work) '
(more than 9 hours in a day receive compensatory time off, which must be used within 30 days.) '
(Weekend work must be approved in advance by the department head.) '
() '
ET
endstream
