(Section 2: Leave Policy) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
0 -24 Td
14 TL
(Every full-time employee receives 20 days of paid annual leave per calendar year. Annual leave) '
(is credited monthly at 1.67 days per month. Up to 10 unused annual leave days can be carried) '
(forward to the next year; any days above 10 expire on 31 December.) '
() '
(Employees also receive 8 days of sick leave per year. Sick leave of more than 2 consecutive) '
(days requires a medical certificate from a registered doctor. Unused sick leave cannot be) '
(carried forward and is not paid out.) '
() '
(There are 10 public holidays each year. The final holiday list is published by HR in the first) '
(week of December for the following year.) '
() '
(Maternity leave is 26 weeks of fully paid leave, as required by Indian law. Paternity leave is) '
(10 working days, which must be taken within 3 months of the child's birth. Adoption leave is 12) '
(weeks for the primary caregiver.) '
() '
(Employees who have completed 2 years of continuous service are eligible for a sabbatical of up) '
(to 3 months. During a sabbatical the employee receives 50 percent of their basic salary. A) '
(sabbatical request must be submitted at least 60 days in advance and requires approval from) '
(both the reporting manager and the HR head.) '
() '
(Bereavement leave of 5 days is granted on the death of an immediate family member. Leave) '
(without pay can be requested for up to 30 days in a year, subject to manager approval.) '
() '
ET
endstream
endobj
