(Section 3: Benefits, Travel and Exit) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
0 -24 Td
14 TL
(All employees are covered by a group health insurance policy with a sum insured of Rs 5 lakh) '
(per year. The policy covers the employee, their spouse, and up to 2 children. Parents can be) '
(added to the policy at the employee's own cost.) '
() '
(Employees receive a learning allowance of Rs 25,000 per financial year for courses,) '
(certifications and books. The allowance is reimbursed after the employee submits a course) '
(completion certificate or receipt. Unused learning allowance does not carry forward.) '
() '
(For business travel, employees at grades L1 to L4 travel by economy class. Employees at grade) '
(L5 and above may travel by business class for flights longer than 4 hours. The daily meal) '
(allowance during business travel is Rs 1,500 within India and USD 60 outside India. Travel) '
(expense claims must be submitted within 15 days of returning.) '
() '
(The notice period is 30 days during probation and 60 days after confirmation. Probation lasts 6) '
(months from the joining date. Employees serving notice cannot take annual leave without manager) '
(approval.) '
() '
(On exit, unused annual leave of up to 15 days is paid out at the basic salary rate. Company) '
(laptops and ID cards must be returned on the last working day. The full and final settlement is) '
(processed within 45 days of the last working day.) '
() '
ET
endstream
